== Part 2: what is left after the moment ratio, the multiplicity and the reduced-mass factor
D    : measured X/H = 0.230487; moment ratio 0.307012 x multiplicity ratio 0.75000 x reduced-mass ratio 1.000817 = 0.230447; left over 1.000171 (Z = 1: the multiplicity and moments account for the whole ratio to 1.7e-04)
3He+ : measured X/H = 6.100827; moment ratio 0.761812 x multiplicity ratio 1.00000 x reduced-mass ratio 1.001088 = 0.762641; left over 7.999603 = Z^p with Z = 2: p = 2.99993

The size dependence nature shows is the density of the electron at the nucleus, |psi(0)|^2 proportional to (Z/a0)^3: an exponent p = 3 in the size of the electron order, measured here as above (secondary frequencies).
Instrument route with the multiplicity added: X/H = (mu_X/mu_p)(mult ratio)(reduced-mass ratio); D: 0.230447 against measured 0.230487
